<title>USA: U.S. High Court allows city billboard ad ban.</title>
<headline>U.S. High Court allows city billboard ad ban.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Supreme Court on Monday rejected a constitutional free-speech challenge to a Baltimore ban on billboards that advertise cigarettes or alcoholic beverages in many public places frequented by children.</p>
<p>The high court's action in the two cases occurred just three days after a federal judge in North Carolina ruled the U.S. Food and Drug Administration can regulate sales and labeling of cigarettes, but has no authority over advertising.</p>
</text>
